{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791818740,"nonce":"VvBI2NdmPHwIBbLHUG/uMcBFPxk=","message":"Decision (review B1): an Anthropic model with no measured history is held at no less than its price with the cached prefix sized from the real rubric, output schema and profile at 3 chars a token and all of it priced as cache writes (screen.cold_price_per_job_usd); the measured mean takes over after the first collect. Each batch stores its admitted hold in score_batch.reserve_per_request_usd (migration 0040) so pending holds are never re-priced lower. Reason: the typical-token hold assumed a 3,900-token always-hit prefix; real prefixes are about 7,100 tokens and batch cache hits are best effort, so a first Sonnet batch could cost about 2x its hold.","files":null}]}